<!--
    kuna: a constant flowing into a return value or call argument whose
    declared type cannot hold a data pointer is not inferred as a pointer.
    dret and cd move the bits of &table into a double (0x404040, the
    denormal 2.08038790635732e-317); they printed (double)table, a
    conversion of an address to a floating value, not the bits.  ebig
    returns the address of msg in a pointer-wide enum and printed it as
    (big)"hello world".

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 const-pointer (p9_emit/coreaction_render.rs,
    ActionConstantPtr check_copy for returns, check_call_input for call
    arguments).  No option.  The rest are controls that must not move: a
    long slot is as wide as a pointer and still prints (long)table; a
    structure passed by value whose member is a pointer still names the
    string; a declared int * return prints table, also with inferconstptr
    off.

    Source (gcc -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -fcf-protection=none, bytes verbatim):

        int table[64] = {1, 2, 3};
        const char msg[] = "hello world";
        struct S { const char *p; };
        enum big { BSMALL = 1, BHUGE = 0x100000000L };
        double td(double v) { return v * 2; }
        double cd(void) { double d; long v = (long)&table[0]; memcpy(&d, &v, 8); return td(d); }
        double dret(void) { double d; long v = (long)&table[0]; memcpy(&d, &v, 8); return d; }
        long tl(long v) { return v + 1; }
        long cl(void) { return tl((long)&table[0]); }
        long laddr(void) { return (long)&table[0]; }
        int *pret(void) { return &table[0]; }
        int takes(struct S s) { return s.p[0]; }
        int cs(void) { struct S s = { msg }; return takes(s); }
        enum big ebig(void) { return (enum big)(uintptr_t)msg; }
-->
